---
# The bounds (MAX_FAULTS, MAX_STOPS, one prompt, one queued message, one
# launch) end every behaviour in a quiet thread with nothing left to do:
# that is rest, not a deadlock.
deadlock_detection: false
---

# Sends whose outcome is ambiguous, or whose client-side state is lost:
# the answer to a POST lost after serve wrote the line, a page reload or
# a session switch while a send or a Stop is in flight, a serve restart.
# One thread's composer (web/src/app.tsx Thread: deliver, the flush
# effect, restoreOnStop, the swallowedByStop timer), App's per-session
# `pending` map, serve's prompt endpoint (api.go prompt -> Supervisor.Send)
# and, as an alternative to the thread's own prompt, one create or
# project message (api.ts create / createThread / messageProject).
#
# THIS SPEC IS THE DESIGN, NOT TODAY'S CODE. Each claim below is one the
# code at the time of writing breaks; where, and how, is listed under
# "Gaps" and is what the MBT and browser stages are expected to show red.
# The mechanisms the spec assumes (none exist yet):
#   R1 every prompt / create / project message carries a client request
#      id; serve records it (in memory while the line is unread, in the
#      input's history entry once it lands, in meta for a create) and a
#      second request with the same id writes nothing and answers ok.
#   R2 a send whose answer never came (fetch failed, the page reloaded,
#      serve restarted) is "unknown", not "Not sent": the page asks serve
#      about the id and only then shows Not sent (server never had it) or
#      Waiting (server has it). A landed input drops any row for its id.
#   R3 what the composer owes a session outlives the Thread and the page:
#      pending rows (accepted flag included), failures, restoreOnStop and
#      stoppedIds are per session in sessionStorage, not React state/refs.
#
# Fields (all on the Session role):
#   serve    "up" | "down" (a restart is Restart then ServeBack)
#   viewing  the page shows this session (a Thread is mounted for it)
#   draft    "msg" (the prompt, typed; or put back after a Stop) | ""
#   status   the row: "idle" | "running"
#   m_req    the prompt's POST: "none" | "out" (serve has not handled it)
#            | "back" (serve handled it; the answer is on its way)
#   m_srv    the prompt at serve: "none" | "unread" (in the child's
#            stdin) | "running" (recorded; its turn is open) | "done"
#            (recorded; the turn ended with a reply, or it landed as a
#            steer) | "cancelled" (recorded; stopped before any reply) |
#            "lost" (written to a child that died before reading it)
#   m_n      how many times the prompt was recorded as an input
#   m_behind the prompt's line was written after the queued message's
#            (a Retry while that one was unread): the child reads it
#            second
#   m_row    the page's own row for it: "none" | "sending" | "waiting"
#            (accepted, unlanded) | "unknown" (answer lost, being
#            checked) | "failed" (the "Not sent" row)
#   m_seen   the transcript on the page shows the recorded input
#   q        the one queued message: "none" | "queued" | "unread"
#            (flushed, written, unlanded) | "turn" (landed as its own
#            turn) | "steer" (landed inside another turn) | "swallowed"
#            (a Stop's cancel ate the line) | "lost" (its child died) |
#            "failed" (a Not sent row)
#   q_n      how many times it was recorded
#   restore  restoreOnStop is armed
#   stop_m, stop_q
#            stoppedIds: a Stop was pressed while this line was unread
#   l        the create / project message: "none" | "out" | "back" |
#            "failed" (an error with Retry) | "done"
#   l_n      sessions (or main-thread messages) serve made for it
#   faults, stops   bounds
#
# Where this departs from the mapped model, and why (verified against
# the code at main 5471918e):
# - `pending` (App state, app.tsx ~5564) survives a session switch; only
#   a reload loses it. restoreOnStop (useRef, ~4346) and stoppedIds
#   (useRef, ~4518) live in the Thread, which is keyed by session
#   (<Thread key={r.id}>), so a SWITCH loses them as surely as a reload:
#   the mapped model only had the reload losing the swallow timer.
# - Failures (bough:failed:<id>) and the queue (bough:queue:<id>) are in
#   sessionStorage and survive both. But a send's error arrives through
#   the Thread that sent it: a request that fails while you are on
#   another session calls the unmounted Thread's setFailures and is lost,
#   while App's setSending still drops its row; the message vanishes.
#   Here responses and losses apply the same viewing or not (R3).
# - A serve restart kills the child, so an accepted line it had not read
#   is gone and its row says Waiting ("accepted") forever: nothing on the
#   page ever lands or fails it. Restart marks such rows unknown (R2).
# - A lost POST is taken to have reached serve completely or not at all
#   (m_req "out" lost = never written). A request that arrives after its
#   client gave up is not modelled.
# - Stop waits for sends in flight (Promise.allSettled(inflight)), so it
#   is enabled only once the prompt's POST is not "out".
# - A Not sent row whose outcome the page cannot know holds the queue
#   (unknown blocks the flush, R2): otherwise the queued head is written
#   behind a prompt the child has not read, and lands as a steer.
# - Retry of a failed queued message is not modelled: its Not sent row is
#   the end of that message here (the liveness claim only needs a row).
# - A Stop that cancels the queued message's own turn does not restore
#   it here (restore is modelled for the prompt only).
# - A walk either sends the thread's prompt or makes one create / project
#   message, never both (Send and the launch actions exclude each
#   other): the two share no state, and carrying a finished launch
#   through every thread state doubled the graph.
#
# Gaps in the code this spec is written against (findings; not fixed
# here):
# G1 api.ts prompt posts {text}; the id stays client-side (app.tsx
#    deliver: "A retry is the same request, so it keeps its id"), so
#    Retry after a lost answer writes the line again: m_n = 2.
# G2 deliver's error path always adds a "Not sent" row, even when the
#    input is already in the transcript; nothing ever reconciles it.
# G3 a reload with a written, unlanded prompt loses `pending`; the flush
#    guard (unlanded.length) passes and the queued head lands as a steer.
# G4 Stop, then switch away and back before it settles: the remounted
#    Thread's restoreOnStop is false; the prompt is never put back.
# G5 a reload (or switch) during the 4 s swallowedByStop timer loses
#    stoppedIds; the swallowed queued message is neither requeued nor
#    reported.
# G6 create / createThread / messageProject carry no id; a Retry (act's
#    toast, ProjectComposer's Send) after a lost answer makes a second
#    session or a second message to main.

# One fault (a lost answer, a reload, a restart) per walk: every gap
# above needs only one, and two took the graph past 3000 states.
MAX_FAULTS = 1
MAX_STOPS = 1

role Session:
    action Init:
        self.serve = "up"
        self.viewing = True
        self.draft = "msg"
        self.status = "idle"
        self.m_req = "none"
        self.m_srv = "none"
        self.m_n = 0
        self.m_row = "none"
        self.m_seen = False
        self.m_behind = False
        self.q = "none"
        self.q_n = 0
        self.restore = False
        self.stop_m = False
        self.stop_q = False
        self.l = "none"
        self.l_n = 0
        self.faults = 0
        self.stops = 0

    # A row of the page's own that is still waiting on the prompt.
    func m_pending():
        return self.m_row in ["sending", "waiting", "unknown"]

    # ---- the person ----

    # Enter on the typed prompt. The thread is idle (the prompt is what
    # starts its turn); a walk that launched does not send (see header).
    atomic action Send:
        require self.viewing and self.draft == "msg"
        require self.m_n == 0 and self.m_srv == "none"
        require self.m_row == "none" and self.m_req == "none"
        require self.l == "none"
        self.draft = ""
        self.m_row = "sending"
        self.m_req = "out"

    # Cmd/Ctrl+Enter while the thread is live: its turn runs, or the
    # prompt is sent and unlanded (app.tsx live = running || unlanded).
    atomic action Enqueue:
        require self.viewing and self.q == "none"
        require self.status == "running" or self.m_row in ["sending", "waiting"]
        self.q = "queued"

    # Retry on the prompt's Not sent row, or on one still being checked
    # (the check needs serve, which may be down): the same request id,
    # so a line serve already has is not written again (R1).
    atomic action Retry:
        require self.viewing and self.m_row in ["failed", "unknown"]
        self.m_row = "sending"
        self.m_req = "out"

    atomic action Discard:
        require self.viewing and self.m_row == "failed"
        self.m_row = "none"

    # Stop (Esc or the button). It waits for a send in flight, then
    # interrupts. A line still unread is held for the child and its turn
    # cancelled at once (stop_m / stop_q), or, for the queued message,
    # the cancel may beat it (StopEatsQueued).
    atomic action Stop:
        require self.viewing and self.serve == "up" and self.stops < MAX_STOPS
        require self.m_req != "out"
        live = (self.status == "running" or self.m_row in ["sending", "waiting"]
                or self.q == "unread")
        require live
        self.stops = self.stops + 1
        self.restore = True
        if self.m_srv == "unread":
            self.stop_m = True
        if self.q == "unread":
            self.stop_q = True
        if self.status == "running":
            self.status = "idle"
            if self.m_srv == "running":
                self.m_srv = "cancelled"

    # A session switch away and back. Nothing the composer owes this
    # session may go with the Thread (R3).
    atomic action SwitchAway:
        require self.viewing
        self.viewing = False

    atomic action SwitchBack:
        require not self.viewing
        self.viewing = True

    # A page reload: requests in flight lose their answers; everything
    # else is kept (R3). An in-flight prompt becomes unknown (R2).
    atomic action ReloadPage:
        require self.viewing and self.faults < MAX_FAULTS
        self.faults = self.faults + 1
        if self.m_req != "none":
            self.m_req = "none"
            if self.m_row == "sending":
                self.m_row = "unknown"
        if self.l in ["out", "back"]:
            self.l = "failed"

    # New session (palette / new-session dialog) or Message the project
    # (the project composer; a Start thread is the same POST). Only in a
    # walk that does not send the thread's prompt; see header.
    atomic action NewSession:
        require self.viewing and self.l == "none"
        require self.m_n == 0 and self.m_row == "none" and self.m_req == "none"
        self.l = "out"

    atomic action MessageProject:
        require self.viewing and self.l == "none"
        require self.m_n == 0 and self.m_row == "none" and self.m_req == "none"
        self.l = "out"

    # The error's Retry (act's toast, or Send again in the project
    # composer): the same request id (R1).
    atomic action RetryLaunch:
        require self.viewing and self.l == "failed"
        self.l = "out"

    # ---- the network and serve ----

    # The prompt's POST reaches serve, which writes the line unless it
    # already has that id (R1).
    atomic fair action ServerWrites:
        require self.serve == "up" and self.m_req == "out"
        if self.m_srv in ["none", "lost"]:
            self.m_srv = "unread"
            self.m_behind = self.q == "unread"
        self.m_req = "back"

    atomic fair action Answer:
        require self.m_req == "back"
        self.m_req = "none"
        if self.m_row == "sending":
            self.m_row = "waiting"

    # The answer never arrives (a proxy, a dropped connection), before or
    # after serve handled the request.
    atomic action ResponseLost:
        require self.m_req != "none" and self.faults < MAX_FAULTS
        self.faults = self.faults + 1
        self.m_req = "none"
        if self.m_row == "sending":
            self.m_row = "unknown"

    # The page asks serve about the id (R2).
    atomic fair action Reconcile:
        require self.serve == "up" and self.m_row == "unknown" and self.m_req == "none"
        if self.m_srv in ["none", "lost"]:
            self.m_row = "failed"
        else:
            self.m_row = "waiting"

    # serve restarts: every child dies with it, requests in flight fail,
    # and rows waiting on a line that died are unknown again (R2).
    atomic action Restart:
        require self.serve == "up" and self.faults < MAX_FAULTS
        self.faults = self.faults + 1
        self.serve = "down"
        self.m_req = "none"
        if self.m_row in ["sending", "waiting"]:
            self.m_row = "unknown"
        if self.m_srv == "unread":
            self.m_srv = "lost"
            self.m_behind = False
        if self.m_srv == "running":
            self.m_srv = "done"
        self.stop_m = False
        if self.q == "unread":
            self.q = "lost"
            self.stop_q = False
        self.status = "idle"
        if self.l in ["out", "back"]:
            self.l = "failed"

    atomic fair action ServeBack:
        require self.serve == "down"
        self.serve = "up"

    # The page learns on reconnect that a flushed line died with its
    # child: a Not sent row (R2).
    atomic fair action ReconcileQueued:
        require self.serve == "up" and self.q == "lost"
        self.q = "failed"

    atomic fair action ServerMakes:
        require self.serve == "up" and self.l == "out"
        if self.l_n == 0:
            self.l_n = 1
        self.l = "back"

    atomic fair action LaunchAnswer:
        require self.l == "back"
        self.l = "done"

    atomic action LaunchLost:
        require self.l in ["out", "back"] and self.faults < MAX_FAULTS
        self.faults = self.faults + 1
        self.l = "failed"

    # ---- the child ----

    # The child records the prompt. After a Stop held for it, its turn is
    # cancelled at once; into a running turn it is a steer. One stdin:
    # lines are read in the order serve wrote them.
    atomic fair action ChildRecordsInput:
        require self.serve == "up" and self.m_srv == "unread"
        require not (self.m_behind and self.q == "unread")
        self.m_n = self.m_n + 1
        self.m_behind = False
        if self.stop_m:
            self.stop_m = False
            self.m_srv = "cancelled"
        elif self.status == "running":
            self.m_srv = "done"
        else:
            self.m_srv = "running"
            self.status = "running"

    # The child records the flushed message, in write order.
    atomic fair action ChildRecordsQueued:
        require self.serve == "up" and self.q == "unread"
        require not (self.m_srv == "unread" and not self.m_behind)
        self.q_n = self.q_n + 1
        if self.stop_q:
            self.stop_q = False
            self.q = "turn"
        elif self.status == "running":
            self.q = "steer"
        else:
            self.q = "turn"
            self.status = "running"

    # The Stop's cancel reaches the child before it read the flushed line
    # (a prompt that reached a child the row had not yet shown running):
    # the line is eaten and no input is ever recorded for it. A race, so
    # not fair: the held path (ChildRecordsQueued) may win it.
    # (A separate action rather than `any` inside Stop: fizz 0.5.3 kept
    # only one branch of that fork.)
    atomic action StopEatsQueued:
        require self.stop_q and self.q == "unread"
        self.q = "swallowed"

    atomic fair action Finish:
        require self.status == "running"
        self.status = "idle"
        if self.m_srv == "running":
            self.m_srv = "done"

    # ---- the page ----

    # The transcript on screen catches up: the recorded input shows, and
    # every row of the page's own for it goes (R2).
    atomic fair action Catchup:
        require self.viewing and self.serve == "up" and not self.m_seen
        require self.m_srv in ["running", "done", "cancelled"]
        self.m_seen = True
        self.m_row = "none"

    # The flush effect: idle, nothing of the prompt's pending or unknown.
    atomic fair action Flush:
        require self.viewing and self.serve == "up" and self.status == "idle"
        require self.q == "queued" and self.m_req == "none"
        pending = self.m_pending()
        require not pending
        self.q = "unread"

    # stoppedPrompt: a prompt stopped before any reply goes back to an
    # empty composer, once the page shows the cancelled turn.
    atomic fair action Restore:
        require self.viewing and self.restore and self.status == "idle"
        require self.m_srv == "cancelled" and self.m_seen
        self.restore = False
        if self.draft == "":
            self.draft = "msg"

    # The swallowedByStop timer: the swallowed message back at the front
    # of the queue.
    atomic fair action Swallow:
        require self.stop_q and self.q == "swallowed" and self.status == "idle"
        self.stop_q = False
        self.q = "queued"

action Init:
    session = Session()

# Retry never delivers the prompt twice (R1).
always assertion PromptRecordedOnce:
    return session.m_n <= 1

# A flushed queued message is recorded once, reloads and Stops included.
always assertion QueuedRecordedOnce:
    return session.q_n <= 1

# A retried create or project message makes one, not two (R1).
always assertion LaunchMadeOnce:
    return session.l_n <= 1

# "Not sent" only for a prompt serve never had: never beside its landed
# input, never for a line a child is about to read (R2).
always assertion NotSentMeansNotSent:
    if session.m_row == "failed":
        return session.m_srv in ["none", "lost"] and not session.m_seen
    return True

# The queue never flushes over an unlanded prompt, reload or not: the
# queued message is always a turn of its own.
always assertion QueuedNeverSteers:
    return session.q != "steer"

# Every sent prompt lands (and shows) or shows a failure row; no row says
# Sending / Waiting forever, a serve restart included. Asked of the page
# only while it shows the session.
always eventually assertion PromptSettles:
    return (not session.viewing) or not (
        session.m_row in ["sending", "waiting", "unknown"]
        or session.q in ["unread", "swallowed", "lost"])

# A prompt stopped before any reply is back in the composer, session
# switches and reloads between the Stop and its settling included.
always eventually assertion StoppedPromptReturns:
    return (not session.viewing) or session.m_srv != "cancelled" or session.draft == "msg"
